.*
.* WRKDSKSTS: each disk unit's size, use and I/O since the display's
.* first look or the last F10. Captured on the primary
.* (tools/conformance/golden/phase12/perf/wrkdsksts*.txt).
.* BLOCKED(phase12): headings and decimal columns sit on a hand grid this renderer does not make (work2_panels::wrkdsksts); it needs a display file with a command line
:PNLGRP.
:CLASS NAME=TIMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 8'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=UNITCL BASETYPE='ZONED 3 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 4'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=SIZECL BASETYPE='ZONED 6 0'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=PCTCL BASETYPE='ZONED 3 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RATECL BASETYPE='ZONED 4 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=RQSCL BASETYPE='ZONED 6 1'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=BUSYCL BASETYPE='ZONED 3 0'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=ELAPSED CLASS=TIMECL.
:VAR NAME=UNIT CLASS=UNITCL.
:VAR NAME=TYPE CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=SIZE CLASS=SIZECL.
:VAR NAME=USED CLASS=PCTCL.
:VAR NAME=IORQS CLASS=RATECL.
:VAR NAME=RQSSIZE CLASS=RQSCL.
:VAR NAME=READRQS CLASS=RATECL.
:VAR NAME=WRITERQS CLASS=PCTCL.
:VAR NAME=READK CLASS=RATECL.
:VAR NAME=WRITEK CLASS=PCTCL.
:VAR NAME=BUSY CLASS=BUSYCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=UNITS VARS='UNIT TYPE SIZE USED IORQS RQSSIZE READRQS WRITERQS READK WRITEK BUSY'.
:KEYL HELP='KEYS/DSKEYS' NAME=DSKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F24 ACTION=MOREKEYS.F24=More keys
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F10 ACTION='RETURN 10'.F10=Restart statistics
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKDSKSTS KEYL=DSKEYS HELP=WRKDSKSTS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=DATETIME.Work with Disk Status
:DATA DEPTH=2 COMPACT.
:DATAI HELP='FLD/ELAPSED' VAR=ELAPSED USAGE=OUTPUT.Elapsed time
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=UNITS MAXHEAD=2.
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/UNIT' VAR=UNIT USAGE=OUTPUT.Unit
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/TYPE' VAR=TYPE USAGE=OUTPUT.Type
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/SIZE' VAR=SIZE USAGE=OUTPUT.Size (G)
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/USED' VAR=USED USAGE=OUTPUT.% Used
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/IORQS' VAR=IORQS USAGE=OUTPUT.I/O Rqs
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/RQSSIZE' VAR=RQSSIZE USAGE=OUTPUT.Request Size (K)
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/READRQS' VAR=READRQS USAGE=OUTPUT.Read Rqs
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/WRITERQS' VAR=WRITERQS USAGE=OUTPUT.Write Rqs
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/READK' VAR=READK USAGE=OUTPUT.Read (K)
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/WRITEK' VAR=WRITEK USAGE=OUTPUT.Write (K)
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/BUSY' VAR=BUSY USAGE=OUTPUT.% Busy
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKDSKSTS.Work with Disk Status - Help
:P.Every disk unit of the system ASP: its size, how full it is and the
requests it served each second since the display first looked or F10
started the measurement over. F5 looks again.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/DSKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F10=Restart statistics
:PD.Starts the statistics over from now.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/ELAPSED'.Elapsed time
:P.The elapsed time shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/UNIT'.Unit
:P.The unit of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:P.The type of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/SIZE'.Size (G)
:P.The size (G) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USED'.% Used
:P.The % Used of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/IORQS'.I/O Rqs
:P.The i/O Rqs of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/RQSSIZE'.Request Size (K)
:P.The request Size (K) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/READRQS'.Read Rqs
:P.The read Rqs of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WRITERQS'.Write Rqs
:P.The write Rqs of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/READK'.Read (K)
:P.The read (K) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WRITEK'.Write (K)
:P.The write (K) of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/BUSY'.% Busy
:P.The % Busy of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
